Day 28: Do You Want to Be Made Well? | Tuesday of the Fourth Week of Lent (Lent Devotional)

📌 YouTube Description
“Do you want to be made well?”
A gentle question.
A piercing question.
A healing question.

Welcome to Day 28 of our Lent journey.
Today’s reflection brings you into the quiet, tender place where Jesus meets the parts of your heart that feel stuck — the wounds you avoid, the fears you carry, the heaviness you can’t name. He does not force His way in. He asks. He invites. He waits for your yes.

This spoken‑word devotional reminds you that healing begins with honesty, not strength. Jesus does not shame your wounds — He restores them. He does not rush your healing — He walks with you through it. Healing is not about worthiness; it is about willingness.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why Jesus asks, “Do you want to be made well?”

How healing begins when you open the hidden places of your heart

Why willingness matters more than perfection

A prayer for courage and restoration

A simple daily activity: whispering, “Lord, heal this place in me.”

